# Nemotron Nano 9B v2 with ITS OWN tool-calling protocol, GPU-forced.
#
# The chain that produced `nemotron-gpu` starts at a RAW LOCAL GGUF
# (Modelfile.nemotron-nano-9b-v2, `FROM E:\models\...gguf`). Ollama assigns a
# RENDERER by architecture in that case, and picked `nemotron-3-nano` -- the
# 4B's, a different generation. The 9B was therefore shown Qwen3-Coder style
# <tool_call><function=...><parameter=...> when it was trained on
# <TOOLCALL>[{json}]</TOOLCALL>. See Modelfile.nemotron9-tools.
#
# That file rules out fixing it with a TEMPLATE override, and is right: a
# Modelfile TEMPLATE does not displace an assigned renderer. What it did not
# test is the model PULLED FROM HUGGING FACE, which carries NVIDIA's real
# template in its manifest and has NO renderer assigned -- nothing to displace.
#
# Measured 2026-09-27, one identical message, num_predict 1, temperature 0:
#
#                                no tools   with tools(1)
#   nemotron-gpu:latest               42           320
#   hf.co/bartowski/...:Q4_K_M        15           234
#
# Different with NO tools at all, so the difference is the template itself and
# not the tool serialisation. The pulled model renders from NVIDIA's template,
# whose 4070 bytes are byte-identical to the chat_template in
# nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-Nano-9B-v2 (sha b7a3a520a4bc1bea, see
# evalkit_store/model_contracts/).
#
# So: FROM the pulled model, add only layer placement. Nothing else.
# num_gpu 99 is a request, not a guarantee -- Ollama clamps to what fits, so
# check `ollama ps` for size_vram against size (M0 findings 1, addendum 3).
FROM hf.co/bartowski/nvidia_NVIDIA-Nemotron-Nano-9B-v2-GGUF:Q4_K_M

PARAMETER num_gpu 99

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OUTCOME, measured 2026-09-27, minutes after the above was written: THIS FILE
# DOES NOT WORK EITHER. Building it is what breaks it.
#
#   ollama create nemotron9-native -f Modelfile.nemotron9-native
#   -> RENDERER: nemotron-3-nano   PARSER: nemotron-3-nano
#   -> template collapses from 4070 chars to 165
#   -> prompt tokens 42 / 320, identical to nemotron-gpu
#
# So `ollama create` re-assigns the renderer by architecture even when FROM a
# pulled model that had none. Modelfile.nemotron9-tools was right about the
# mechanism and understated it: it is not only that a TEMPLATE cannot displace
# an assigned renderer, it is that CREATING A MODEL AT ALL assigns one.
#
# The correct template therefore survives only in the pulled model itself,
# which we must use unbuilt:
#
#   LATTICE_EVAL_MODEL=hf.co/bartowski/nvidia_NVIDIA-Nemotron-Nano-9B-v2-GGUF:Q4_K_M
#
# Layer placement then has nowhere to live in a Modelfile, which is why
# LATTICE_NUM_GPU was added to ollama_client.py and goes in the API options.
#
# This file is kept as the record of the attempt. Do not build it. The ollama
# model it produced was deleted, because a model named "native" that is not
# native is a trap.
